    "Recorded through PeriHub's real HID++ code (MouseTask::open through receiver slot 1, HidppDevice, the recorder) from a simulated mouse, g903_hero() in mouse.rs, that answers with the bytes of the transcript in the report of issue #115: name, device info (unit id left out), firmware, feature table with types and versions, onboard memory (format 4, 16 sectors of 255 bytes, 12 buttons), DPI range, polling rates, the profile list sector byte for byte (profile 1 enabled, 2 to 5 disabled, CRC 40 37) and the active profile. the_replay_of_the_g903_hero_is_what_perihub_records_of_it writes this file again with PERIHUB_WRITE_TRANSCRIPTS=1.",
    "PeriHub 0.9.7 did not read 0x8071, so the report's own transcript cannot replay the reading of a newer version. The 0x8071 answers for the zone count and the two zones (location 1 and location 2, 4 effects each) are those a G903 HERO sent on its cable in libratbag issue #774 (2019). Made up: the ids of the effects of each zone (off, fixed, colour cycle, breathing), which neither source has; a new report will show the real ones. The root feature's answers carry the feature's index only, without the type and version the real mouse adds after it."
